      "A dwelling unit is used 'by one family'. Family means relatives, or not more than five unrelated persons, with single cooking facilities (232-6)",
      "Lot area and density rules count dwelling units. R-1 needs 12,000 sq ft per family and caps density at 2.5 units per acre (232-153)",
      "The R-3A district allows duplex dwellings only. It is the closest two-unit option, not an ADU path (232-196)",
      "An accessory structure footprint in a residential district may not exceed 25% of the principal building footprint (232-6 'Accessory structure')",
